          %p
            Furthermore, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+ring"} Noetherian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent modules
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{Spec R}
            and finitely generated modules over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %h2#statement_in_the_formalism_of_functor_of_points Statement in the formalism of functor of points
          %p
            In the formalism of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"} functor of points
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            (with the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec
            now being tautologically defined as the identity functor), and the category of quasicoherent modules over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
            is now defined as the category of
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            of categories over the site of affine schemes with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
          %p
            The functor of points approach carries over to quasicoherent modules over non-affine schemes: given such a scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the stack of quasicoherent modules defined above. In concrete terms, this boils down to picking an open cover of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and defining a quasicoherent module using
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                cocycle data
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cocycle+data"} ?
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre-Swan+theorem"} Serre-Swan theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+algebra+and+geometry"} duality between algebra and geometry
          %h2#references References
          %p The result is originally due to:
          %ul
            %li#Serre55
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Pierre+Serre"}> Jean-Pierre Serre
              , §48 &amp; §49 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Faisceaux Algebriques Coherents
              %strong 61
              2 (1955) 197. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1969915"}> doi:10.2307/1969915
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p It appears in many texts (often without a name, but elsewhere in the nLab it is referred to as the “affine Serre theorem”), for example:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Hartshorne"}> Robin Hartshorne
                , Chapter II, Corollary 5.5 in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 52
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-3849-0"} doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-3849-0
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Stacks+Project"}> The Stacks Project
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01IB"} Lemma 26.7.5
          .property
            category:
            = succeed "," do
              %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/algebra"} algebra
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
